WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.032
A generative decoder should not see future tokens while predicting the next one.

00:00:05.032 --> 00:00:13.387
Causal masking enforces that rule by allowing a position to attend only to itself and earlier positions.

00:00:13.387 --> 00:00:18.527
That restriction is what makes next-token generation autoregressive.

00:00:18.527 --> 00:00:25.507
If the model could see the future token during training, next-token prediction would become a cheating problem.

00:00:25.507 --> 00:00:28.547
The mask prevents that information leak.
